  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">OECD/DAC Guidance on donor support, engaging Civil Society &amp; PWB 2017-2023 - OECD/DAC continued support CS PWB workstream 2020-2023</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">OECD/DAC V&#xE4;gledning om givarst&#xF6;d, engagerande civilsamh&#xE4;lle och PWB 2017-2023</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Insatsen utg&#xF6;r ett st&#xF6;d till resultatomr&#xE5;de 15 i OECD/DAC Programme of Work and Budget (PWB) 2017-2018. Resultatomr&#xE5;det &#xE4;r inriktat p&#xE5; att OECD/DAC b&#xE4;ttre ska ta tillvara den kunskap och kapacitet som NGOs och det &#xF6;vriga civila samh&#xE4;llet spelar inom utvecklingssamarbetet.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sida supports output 15 of OECD/DAC Programme of Work and Budget (PWB) 2017-2018. The aim is for OECD/DAC to improve its ability to take advantage of the knowledge and the capacity that rests with NGOs and the civil society at large in the field of development cooperation.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">&quot;Increased legitimacy and impact of OECD norms and standards on sustainable development through more strategic engagement with civil society. 
Development agencies of provider countries, in collaboration with civil society organisations, provide more effective support to civil society organisations to achieve key SDGs focused on the most vulnerable poor people in developing countries.&quot;

The civil society workstream in the DAC PWB 2021-23, sets out a new programme that builds on the groundwork and achievements of the OECDs work under the DACcivil society workstream to date:
- To sustain and further widen and mainstream the implementation of the DAC-CSO Dialogue Framework through regular, more systematic engagement with civil society.
- Drawing from the findings of the 2020 study, Foresight Policy Paper, and other sources, and through a transparent and inclusive consultation process, to produce a new policy document (recommendation or uidance) to improve DAC member contributions to the promotion of enabling environments for civil society.</narrative>
  </description>
